            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Lily is making a drink by mixing water and cordial. She starts by making 5.4 L of drink using a ratio of ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "35:1",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". However, the instructions say she should use the ratio of ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "20:1",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". How much more cordial should she add to her current mixture so that the ratio is correct?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "112.5 mL more cordial.",
      "worked": "Initially, water : cordial is $35:1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Total parts} &= 35+1=36\\\\\n36\\text{ parts} &= 5.4\\text{ L}\\\\\n1\\text{ part} &= 5.4\\div36=0.15\\text{ L}\\\\\n\\text{Water} &= 35\\times0.15=5.25\\text{ L}\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe water stays at 5.25 L. For the required ratio $20:1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n20\\text{ parts} &= 5.25\\text{ L}\\\\\n1\\text{ part} &= 5.25\\div20=0.2625\\text{ L}\\\\\n\\text{Extra cordial} &= 0.2625-0.15=0.1125\\text{ L}\\\\\n\\text{Extra cordial} &= 0.1125\\times1000=112.5\\text{ mL}\n\\end{align*}$$\nLily should add 112.5 mL of cordial.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
